      "detailed_figure_description": "Hand-drawn simple circuit consisting of a battery on the left connected by a rectangular wire loop. The battery’s upper terminal is marked positive and its lower terminal negative; an orange V labels the voltage. Blue arrows marked I show conventional current moving clockwise around the loop. Black arrows and e⁻ labels show electrons moving in the opposite direction, counterclockwise, including downward through the battery.",
